      "tag": "Find",
      "h2": "Two Research Types",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Primary research</strong> means YOU collect data — surveys, interviews, observing. <strong>Secondary</strong> means using existing data — websites, books, magazines. Use both.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Specify",
      "h2": "Writing a Spec",
      "body_html": "<p>A <strong>specification</strong> turns the brief into hard requirements. 'Must hold 1.5 kg', 'Must fit in a 30 cm box', 'Must cost under £10'. Be specific or you can't tell if you've succeeded.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "SMART",
      "h2": "SMART Goals",
      "body_html": "<p>Specification points should be <strong>SMART</strong> — Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Realistic, Time-bound. 'Looks good' isn't SMART; 'matches 3 user colours' is.</p>"
    }
  ],
